@page "/walkThrough"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<h3>Application Walkthrough</h3>

<Tabs EnableFadeEffect="true" Class="demo-tabs" NavStyle="NavStyle.Underline">
    <Tab Title="Main Dashboard" IsActive="true">
    <Content>
        <div class="demo-content">

            <h4 class="mt-3">Main Dashboard</h4>

            <p>
                The Main Dashboard provides a quick overview of the user's MyHome data.
                It displays the total number of registered real estates and devices,
                together with the most recently added property and device.
                It also highlights the device with the nearest upcoming warranty
                expiration, allowing important information to be seen immediately
                after signing in.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/MainDashboard.png"
                   Alt="MyHome Main Dashboard" />

            <h4 class="mt-5">Quick Navigation</h4>

            <p>
                Each dashboard card also provides direct access to the corresponding
                section of the application. Users can quickly open their account,
                real estates, devices, or warranties without navigating through
                multiple pages.
            </p>

        </div>
    </Content>
</Tab>
   <Tab Title="Real Estates">
    <Content>
        <div class="demo-content">

            <h4 class="mt-3">Real Estate Management</h4>

            <p>
                MyHome allows users to manage multiple real estates within a single
                account. Each property stores its own name and address information
                and acts as a container for the devices assigned to that location.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/RealEstateManagement.png"
                   Alt="Real Estate Management" />


            <h4 class="mt-5">Add a Real Estate</h4>

            <p>
                Users can add a new property by entering its name and address.
                Once created, devices can be assigned to the property.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/AddRealEstate.png"
                   Alt="Add Real Estate" />


            <h4 class="mt-5">Edit a Real Estate</h4>

            <p>
                Existing property information can be updated at any time,
                allowing the user to change the property name or address.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/EditRealEstate.png"
                   Alt="Edit Real Estate" />


            <h4 class="mt-5">Deleting a Real Estate</h4>

            <p>
                Deleting a real estate requires additional handling when devices
                are still assigned to it. Instead of automatically deleting those
                devices together with the property, MyHome allows the user to decide
                what should happen to them.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/DeleteRealEstate.png"
                   Alt="Delete Real Estate" />


            <h4 class="mt-5">Keep or Reassign Devices</h4>

            <p>
                When a property contains devices, they can be kept as unassigned
                devices or moved to another existing real estate before the property
                is deleted. This prevents device information from being lost.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/DeleteRealEstateWithDevices.png"
                   Alt="Keep or Reassign Devices When Deleting Real Estate" />

        </div>
    </Content>
</Tab>
   <Tab Title="Devices">
    <Content>
        <div class="demo-content">

            <h4 class="mt-3">Device Management</h4>

            <p>
                The Devices section provides an overview of all registered devices.
                Users can view device information, search for devices, and access
                actions for editing, deleting, generating QR codes, and creating emails.
                Devices are connected to real estates and can be managed individually.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/Devices.png"
                   Alt="Device Management" />


            <h4 class="mt-5">Edit Device</h4>

            <p>
                Device information can be updated at any time. Users can edit details
                such as the device name, type, manufacturer, model, serial number,
                IP address, MAC address, and assigned real estate.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/DeviceEdit.png"
                   Alt="Edit Device Details" />


            <h4 class="mt-5">Delete Device</h4>

            <p>
                Before a device is permanently removed, MyHome displays a confirmation
                dialog to help prevent accidental deletion.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/DeviceDelete.png"
                   Alt="Delete Device Confirmation" />


            <h4 class="mt-5">Device QR Codes</h4>

            <p>
                MyHome can generate QR codes for registered devices. Each QR code
                provides a quick way to identify a physical device and access its
                information in the application.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/DeviceQrLabels.png"
                   Alt="Generated Device QR Codes" />


            <h4 class="mt-5">Print QR Codes</h4>

            <p>
                Generated QR codes can be prepared for printing directly from the
                application, making it possible to create physical labels for devices
                around the property.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/DeviceQrPrint.png"
                   Alt="Print Device QR Codes" />


            <h4 class="mt-5">Create Device Email</h4>

            <p>
                Users can select device information and generate an email containing
                the relevant details. This can be useful when contacting a retailer,
                manufacturer, service company, or other support provider.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/DeviceEmailSelection.png"
                   Alt="Select Device Information for Email" />


            <h4 class="mt-5">Generated Email</h4>

            <p>
                MyHome automatically prepares the selected device information in an
                email, reducing the need to manually copy model numbers, serial numbers,
                and other device details.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/DeviceEmailCreated.png"
                   Alt="Generated Device Email" />

        </div>
    </Content>
</Tab>
    <Tab Title="Devices Warranties">
    <Content>
        <div class="demo-content">

            <h4 class="mt-3">Device Warranty Management</h4>

            <p>
                The Device Warranties section keeps warranty and purchase information
                connected to each registered device. Users can store the purchase date,
                warranty period, extended warranty information, receipts, and insurance
                documents. This makes it easier to find important documentation and
                monitor upcoming warranty expiration dates.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/DeviceWarranties.png"
                   Alt="Device Warranty Management" />


            <h4 class="mt-5">Edit Warranty Details</h4>

            <p>
                Warranty information can be updated directly from the warranty overview.
                Users can change the purchase date, warranty length, and extended warranty
                period. MyHome automatically calculates the warranty expiration date based
                on the stored warranty information.
            </p>

            <p>
                Warranty receipts and extended warranty documents can also be uploaded
                and stored with the device. Existing documents can be opened or replaced,
                keeping purchase and warranty documentation easily accessible in one place.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/Images/DemoImages/EditDeviceWarranty.png"
                   Alt="Edit Device Warranty Details" />

        </div>
    </Content>
</Tab>
    <Tab Title="Shop Details">
    <Content>
        <div class="demo-content">

            <h4 class="mt-3">Shop Details</h4>

            <p>
                Purchase shop information is connected to registered devices.
                Users can view and update the shop name, website, phone number
                and address, keeping purchase information together with the
                corresponding device and warranty data.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/images/demoImages/ShopDetails.png"
                   Alt="Device Shop Details" />

        </div>
    </Content>
</Tab>
    <Tab Title="Wifi QR Code">
    <Content>
        <div class="demo-content">

            <h4 class="mt-3">Wi-Fi QR Code Generator</h4>

            <p>
                MyHome includes a tool for generating a QR code from a Wi-Fi
                network name and password. The generated QR code can be scanned
                by another device to simplify connecting to the network.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/images/demoImages/WifiQrCode.png"
                   Alt="Wi-Fi QR Code Generator" />

        </div>
    </Content>
</Tab>
    <Tab Title="User Management">
        <Content>
            <div class="demo-content">

                <h4 class="mt-3">User Management Dashboard</h4>

                <p>
                    Administrators can manage registered users from a dedicated dashboard.
                    Users can be searched, assigned roles, deleted, or temporarily accessed
                    for support and troubleshooting.
                </p>

                <Image Src="/images/demoImages/UserManagement.png"
                       Alt="User Management Dashboard" />

                <h4 class="mt-5">Role Management</h4>

                <p>
                    Administrators can change a user's role directly from the user management
                    dashboard. Role-based authorization is implemented using ASP.NET Core Identity.
                </p>

                <Image Src="/images/demoImages/RoleManagement.png"
                       Alt="User Role Management" />

                <h4 class="mt-5">Delete User</h4>

                <p>
                    User deletion requires confirmation before the account is removed,
                    helping prevent accidental administrative actions.
                </p>

                <Image Src="/images/demoImages/DeleteUser.png"
                       Alt="Delete User Confirmation" />

                <h4 class="mt-5">Login as User</h4>

                <p>
                    Administrators can temporarily access the application as another user
                    for support and troubleshooting. While impersonation mode is active,
                    a visible banner identifies the current user and provides an option
                    to return to the administrator account.
                </p>

                <Image Src="/images/demoImages/Impersonation.png"
                       Alt="Administrator Impersonation Mode" />

            </div>
        </Content>
    </Tab>
    <Tab Title="User Account">
    <Content>
        <div class="demo-content">

            <h4 class="mt-3">Account Overview</h4>

            <p>
                Users can manage their personal account information from the account
                area. The overview also displays a summary of the user's registered
                real estates and devices.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/images/demoImages/UserProfile.png"
                   Alt="User Account Profile" />

            <h4 class="mt-5">Email Management</h4>

            <p>
                Users can view their current email address and update it through
                the account management interface.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/images/demoImages/UserEmail.png"
                   Alt="User Email Management" />

            <h4 class="mt-5">Password Management</h4>

            <p>
                Users can securely change their password by providing their current
                password and confirming the new password.
            </p>

            <Image Src="/images/demoImages/UserPassword.png"
                   Alt="User Password Management" />

        </div>
    </Content>
</Tab>
</Tabs>
<footer class="demo-footer">
    <div class="container text-center py-4">

        <p class="mb-2">
            MyHome — C# / .NET / Blazor Portfolio Project
        </p>

        <a href="https://github.com/LySeriuos/MyHome"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener noreferrer"
           class="me-3">
            <i class="bi bi-github"></i>
            GitHub
        </a>

        <a href="YOUR_LINKEDIN_URL"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <i class="bi bi-linkedin"></i>
            LinkedIn
        </a>

    </div>
</footer>
<style>
    .demo-content {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin-top: 20px;
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
}

.demo-content h3 {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.demo-content h4 {
    margin-top: 40px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.demo-content p {
    max-width: 900px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.demo-screenshot {
    display: block;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid #ddd;
    border-radius: 6px;
    box-shadow: 0 3px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
}
.demo-footer {
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;

    min-height: 55px;
    padding: 12px 20px;

    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 25px;

    background-color: white;
    border-top: 1px solid #dee2e6;

    z-index: 1000;
}

.demo-footer a {
    text-decoration: none;
}

.demo-tabs .nav-tabs {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dee2e6;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 25px;
}

.demo-tabs .nav-link {
    border: 1px solid #d8e3e8;
    border-radius: 12px 12px 0 0;

    padding: 10px 22px;

    background-color: #edf4f7;
    color: #495057;

    font-weight: 500;

    transition: all 0.2s ease;
}

/* Mouse hover */
.demo-tabs .nav-link:hover {
    background-color: #e1edf2;
    color: #212529;
}

/* Selected tab */
.demo-tabs .nav-link.active {
    background-color: #efdcd3;
    color: #212529;

    border-color: #efdcd3;
    font-weight: 600;
}
</style>

